{
  "$Comment": "Hot Cocoa, the second of the three Christmas treats: made at a Chef's Stove (the Cookingbench, its Prepared tab, where the game files its finished dishes; it has no drinks tab) once a player has learned it from Christmas_Recipe_Hot_Cocoa. It wears the game's wooden mug (Deco_Mug's model, texture and icon), and PlayerAnimationsId swaps the eating animation for the mug's own drink, with the mug's drinking sounds (ConsumeSFX, ConsumedSFX). Drinking it gives an instant heal, Christmas_Food_Regen (the game's top food regen, for ten minutes) and Christmas_Food_Warmth (40% less Ice damage); it clears the game's own food regens first, so they never stack from this side. Its description in items.lang writes the numbers out: change it with the effects. The recipe takes a tankard of water the way the game's dough does and hands the empty Deco_Tankard back as its second output. The drink is good all year.",
